## 22. DATABASE SECURITY AND ROW-LEVEL SECURITY

Enable Supabase Row-Level Security on every table exposed through the application API.

Write and test policies that enforce the following:

- Public visitors can read only publicly available listings and approved public profile fields.
- Authenticated users can manage their own profiles within permitted fields.
- Users can modify only their own listings.
- Private or removed listings are not exposed as public listings.
- Users can access only their own favourites.
- Swap participants can access only the offers and transactions in which they are authorized participants.
- Only authorized conversation participants can read messages.
- Only authenticated participants can send messages to their conversations.
- Users cannot mark another participant's messages as their own.
- Users cannot alter their role to administrator.
- Users cannot edit their own reviews after submission unless an explicitly designed moderation workflow allows it.
- Users cannot create false transaction confirmations for other participants.
- Users cannot modify transaction records in ways that bypass valid state transitions.
- Only authorized administrators can perform administrative operations.

Use trusted server-side functions or appropriately secured database functions for operations that require atomicity or elevated permissions.

Do not trust user-supplied IDs, prices, roles, ownership claims, or status values without server-side validation.

