## 27. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

Implement these rules throughout the application:

1. A user cannot make a swap offer to themselves.
2. A user cannot offer an item they do not own.
3. A user cannot make an offer using an inactive or unavailable listing.
4. A user cannot accept an offer for a listing they do not control.
5. Only the intended recipient can accept or decline an incoming offer.
6. Only authorized participants can counter-offer or withdraw their own pending offers.
7. Cash amounts must be valid non-negative numbers.
8. Cash top-up direction must be explicit.
9. Accepted swaps must preserve the accepted terms.
10. Competing accepted transactions must not reserve the same listing simultaneously.
11. Both parties must confirm before an exchange is marked completed.
12. Only completed transactions permit transaction-based reviews.
13. Blocked users must not be able to initiate new interactions that the blocking rules prohibit.
14. Suspended users must not be able to create listings or initiate new offers.
15. Deleted, expired, or unavailable listings must be handled consistently across search, offers, and transactions.
16. Administrators must not be able to silently alter transaction history without an auditable record.

Use server-side authorization and transactional database operations for sensitive workflows.

